'''''Saxifraga granulata''''', commonly called '''meadow saxifrage''',<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17}}</ref> is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Saxifragaceae]].<ref name="GBIF">{{cite web|url=https://www.gbif.org/species/7339311|title=Saxifraga granulata Hook.f. & Thomson|work=GBIF Backbone Taxonomy|publisher=[[Global Biodiversity Information Facility]]|accessdate=9 January 2014|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20140109181634/http://www.gbif.org/species/7339311|url-status=live|archivedate=9 January 2014}}</ref> It is native to most of Europe and Morocco.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Saxifraga granulata |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:793749-1 |access-date=June 24, 2022 |website=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew}}</ref>

== Taxonomy==
''Saxifraga granulata'' was first [[Species description|formally described]] by [[Carl Linnaeus|Linnaeus]] as part of his original description of ''Saxifraga'' in ''[[Species Plantarum]]'' in 1753.<ref>[[D. A. Webb|Webb DA]] (1993) Saxifragaceae.  In: Tutin TG, et al. (eds.). ''[[Flora Europaea]]'' (2nd ed.) 1:437–459. [https://books.google.com/books?id=XkI3UttRP6QC&dq=granulata&pg=PA450 p. 450] {{ISBN|9780521410076}}.</ref> ''S. granulata'' is the [[type species]] of the genus ''Saxifraga''.<ref>
Gornall RJ (1987) An outline of a revised classification of ''Saxifraga'' L. ''Botanical Journal of the Linnean Society'' 95:273–292. {{doi|10.1111/j.1095-8339.1987.tb01860.x}}</ref>

